key_decisions.decision:
Migrations stay forward-only, embedded and tracked by user_version, one transaction each, and they now run under possession:
- a separate *sql.DB with one connection;
- foreign_keys OFF before BEGIN;
- foreign_key_check before COMMIT, where any row means rollback;
- foreign_keys ON deferred;
- the handle closed before the serving pool, which has foreign_keys(1), is opened.

contracts.error_cases:
Exit 2, with one stderr block naming every bad variable, before the DB opens or a port binds:
- HBAND_OWNER_GITHUB_ID missing, or any of "", "0", "-1", "+5", " 5", "5 ", "05", "octocat", "@octocat", "a@b.c", "1e5", "12.0", "9223372036854775808";
- client ID or secret missing or empty;
- HBAND_BASE_URL, HBAND_GITHUB_URL or HBAND_GITHUB_API_URL not absolute, http on a non-loopback host, or carrying a path other than '/', a query, a fragment or userinfo;
- HBAND_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES (once SC-002 adds it) not matching `^[1-9][0-9]*$` or above 209715200.

Exit 1 if the data dir cannot be created, the DB cannot be opened (including a newer schema or a migration whose foreign_key_check returns rows), or the listen fails.

contracts.notes:
GET /admin answers the owner 200 with the data-hband-admin marker and no redirect. After SC-002 it also carries the upload form's `<input type="file">`, which the finish line checks.

The matrix is driven in-process with ServeHTTP and httptest.NewRequest, so the request target is passed through verbatim and no redirect is followed:
- cleaned: //admin/, /admin/../admin/, //admin get 301 to the clean path;
- case: /ADMIN, /ADMIN/ get 404;
- gated: /admin, /admin/, /%61dmin, /%61dmin/, /admin/%2e%2e/admin/, /admin/does-not-exist and every adminRoutes path get the outcomes above.

The invariant holds over every anonymous and non-owner response: no 2xx, no marker, and any Location is /admin, /admin/ or begins /auth/github/login?.

cases.shape:
No cookie. Every path variant class, under GET, HEAD and POST:
- cleaned: //admin/, /admin/../admin/, //admin get 301 to the clean path;
- case: /ADMIN, /ADMIN/ get 404;
- gated: /admin, /admin/, /%61dmin, /%61dmin/, /admin/%2e%2e/admin/, /admin/does-not-exist and every adminRoutes path get 303 to login for GET and HEAD, and 403 for POST.

No response is 2xx or carries the marker. Every Location is /admin, /admin/ or /auth/github/login?..., and every gate response carries Cache-Control: no-store.

Four sessions:
- one minted while the owner was 42, after the handler is rebuilt on the same DB with owner 43;
- one expired, by an injected clock moved past expires_at;
- one malformed (not 43 base64url characters, so no DB query runs);
- one rotated away by a new sign-in.

The first gets 403 on /admin and is still signed in. The others are anonymous (303 to login).

The store is closed at three moments:
- before a callback that would succeed: 503, no hband_sid Set-Cookie, a hband_oauth clear present, and zero sessions rows after reopening;
- before logout: 503 and no hband_sid Set-Cookie;
- after sign-in, with the owner's cookie: /admin 503 with no marker, GET / 200 as anonymous, /healthz 503.

outside_claims.claim:
http.DetectContentType results:
- application/zip for PK\x03\x04 and image/png for PNG;
- text/html; charset=utf-8 for input starting <!doctype html>;
- text/plain; charset=utf-8 for UTF-8 text with a BOM, and for HTML that starts with a tag outside its list, such as <meta>.
